IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`
IMPORT `oa1-helpers`

-- Old Age Security Act, Part I, "Payment of Pension": when payment commences (s 8(1), (2), (2.1)), how long it lasts
-- (s 8(3)), when it is suspended (s 9), when the pensioner may ask for it to stop and start again (s 9.1), when it
-- resumes after incarceration (s 9.2), and the pensioner's request to cancel it (s 9.3).
-- A month is any date in it; every rule normalises with the core's `the first day of the month containing`.
-- The earlier effective dates of ss 8(1) and 8(2) are "as may be prescribed by regulation" (Regulations s 5, piece oa3),
-- and the times of s 9.3 are "prescribed" (Regulations s 26.1, piece oa3): each is an input.

§ `Payment of Pension`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 8(1): commencement of payment

-- "where an application is approved after the last day of the month in which it was received, the approval may be effective as of
-- such earlier date, not prior to the day on which the application was received, as may be prescribed by regulation."
-- src:189 | Commencement of pension
-- src:190 | 8 (1) Payment of pension to any person shall commence in the first month after the application therefor has been approved, but where an application is approved after the last day of the month in which it was received, the approval may be effective as of such earlier date, not prior to the day on which the application was received, as may be prescribed by regulation.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 8(1) (src:189-190)
GIVEN received IS A DATE
      approved IS A DATE
      `the earlier day as of which the approval is to be effective` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 8(1): the approval may be effective as of the earlier day` received approved `the earlier day as of which the approval is to be effective` MEANS
        approved GREATER THAN (`the last day of the month containing` received)
    AND `the earlier day as of which the approval is to be effective` AT LEAST received
    AND `the earlier day as of which the approval is to be effective` LESS THAN approved

-- s 8(2): "Notwithstanding subsection (1), where a person who has applied to receive a pension attained the age of sixty-five years
-- before the day on which the application was received, the approval of the application may be effective as of such earlier day, not
-- before the later of (a) a day one year before the day on which the application was received, and (b) the day on which the
-- applicant attained the age of sixty-five years, as may be prescribed by regulation."
-- src:191 | Exception
-- src:192 | (2) Notwithstanding subsection (1), where a person who has applied to receive a pension attained the age of sixty-five years before the day on which the application was received, the approval of the application may be effective as of such earlier day, not before the later of
-- src:193 | (a) a day one year before the day on which the application was received, and
-- src:194 | (b) the day on which the applicant attained the age of sixty-five years,
-- src:195 | as may be prescribed by regulation.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 8(2) (src:191-195)
GIVEN birth IS A DATE
      received IS A DATE
      `the earlier day as of which the approval is to be effective` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 8(2): the approval may be effective as of the earlier day` birth received `the earlier day as of which the approval is to be effective` MEANS
        (`the day on which a person born on` birth `attains the age of` 65) LESS THAN received
    AND `the earlier day as of which the approval is to be effective`
            AT LEAST (`oa1: the later of two dates` (`the day that is` (`a limit in years` 1) `before` received) (`the day on which a person born on` birth `attains the age of` 65))
    AND `the earlier day as of which the approval is to be effective` LESS THAN received

-- The day as of which the approval is effective: the earlier day if s 8(1) or s 8(2) allows it, otherwise the day of approval.
-- src:189 | Commencement of pension
-- src:190 | 8 (1) Payment of pension to any person shall commence in the first month after the application therefor has been approved, but where an application is approved after the last day of the month in which it was received, the approval may be effective as of such earlier date, not prior to the day on which the application was received, as may be prescribed by regulation.
-- src:191 | Exception
-- src:192 | (2) Notwithstanding subsection (1), where a person who has applied to receive a pension attained the age of sixty-five years before the day on which the application was received, the approval of the application may be effective as of such earlier day, not before the later of
-- src:193 | (a) a day one year before the day on which the application was received, and
-- src:194 | (b) the day on which the applicant attained the age of sixty-five years,
-- src:195 | as may be prescribed by regulation.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, ss 8(1), 8(2) (src:189-195)
GIVEN birth IS A DATE
      received IS A DATE
      approved IS A DATE
      -- out of range: section 5 (piece oa3): Regulations, the earlier day of effect
      `the earlier day as of which the approval is to be effective, as prescribed` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 8: the day as of which the approval is effective` birth received approved `the earlier day as of which the approval is to be effective, as prescribed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the earlier day as of which the approval is to be effective, as prescribed`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN approved
    WHEN JUST earlier THEN
        IF     `s 8(2): the approval may be effective as of the earlier day` birth received earlier
            OR `s 8(1): the approval may be effective as of the earlier day` received approved earlier
        THEN earlier
        ELSE approved

-- "Payment of pension to any person shall commence in the first month after the application therefor has been approved":
-- the first day of the month after the month containing the day as of which the approval is effective.
-- Where approval is effective as of an earlier day, "the first month after the application has been approved" is counted from that day (fork OA1-F18 of NOTES.md).
-- src:189 | Commencement of pension
-- src:190 | 8 (1) Payment of pension to any person shall commence in the first month after the application therefor has been approved, but where an application is approved after the last day of the month in which it was received, the approval may be effective as of such earlier date, not prior to the day on which the application was received, as may be prescribed by regulation.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 8(1) (src:189-190)
GIVEN `the day as of which the approval is effective` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 8(1): the month in which payment of the pension commences` `the day as of which the approval is effective` MEANS
    `the first day of the month that is` 1 `months after the month containing` `the day as of which the approval is effective`

-- s 8(2.1): "Despite subsection (1), if the application by a person described in subsection 5(3) is approved while that person is
-- incarcerated, payment of their pension shall commence in respect of the month in which they are released but only after they
-- notify the Minister in writing before or after their release." NOTHING: payment has not commenced (no notice yet, or not yet released).
-- src:196 | Incarcerated persons
-- src:197 | (2.1) Despite subsection (1), if the application by a person described in subsection 5(3) is approved while that person is incarcerated, payment of their pension shall commence in respect of the month in which they are released but only after they notify the Minister in writing before or after their release.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 8(2.1) (src:196-197)
GIVEN `the application by a person described in subsection 5(3) is approved while that person is incarcerated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the person is released` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the person notifies the Minister in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month in which payment would commence under subsection 8(1)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 8(2.1): the month in respect of which payment of the pension commences` `the application by a person described in subsection 5(3) is approved while that person is incarcerated` `the day on which the person is released` `the person notifies the Minister in writing` `the month in which payment would commence under subsection 8(1)` MEANS
    IF `the application by a person described in subsection 5(3) is approved while that person is incarcerated`
    THEN (CONSIDER `the day on which the person is released`
          WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
          WHEN JUST released THEN
              IF `the person notifies the Minister in writing`
              THEN JUST (`the first day of the month containing` released)
              ELSE NOTHING)
    ELSE JUST `the month in which payment would commence under subsection 8(1)`

-- s 8(3): "the pension shall continue to be paid during the lifetime of the pensioner and shall cease with the payment for the
-- month in which the pensioner dies": the last month paid is the month of death.
-- src:198 | Duration
-- src:199 | (3) Subject to this Act, the pension shall continue to be paid during the lifetime of the pensioner and shall cease with the payment for the month in which the pensioner dies.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 8(3) (src:198-199)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `the day on which the pensioner dies` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 8(3): the pension is still paid for the month` month `the day on which the pensioner dies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day on which the pensioner dies`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST died THEN `the first day of the month containing` month AT MOST `the first day of the month containing` died

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 9: suspension

-- s 9(1): absent from Canada. The six consecutive months are those after the month in which the pensioner left Canada ("exclusive of
-- the month in which the pensioner left") and after becoming a pensioner; payment is suspended for the months after those six while
-- the absence continues, and may resume with the month of return (fork OA1-F8 of NOTES.md: the month the count starts from when the
-- pensioner left before becoming a pensioner).
-- src:200 | Suspension of pension where pensioner leaves Canada
-- src:201 | 9 (1) Where a pensioner, having left Canada either before or after becoming a pensioner, has remained outside Canada after becoming a pensioner for six consecutive months, exclusive of the month in which the pensioner left Canada, payment of the pension for any period the pensioner continues to be absent from Canada after those six months shall be suspended, but payment may be resumed with the month in which the pensioner returns to Canada.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 9(1) (src:200-201)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `the month in which the pensioner left Canada` IS A DATE
      `the month in which the person became a pensioner` IS A DATE
      `the month in which the pensioner returns to Canada` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(1): the pensioner has been absent from Canada and payment for the month falls to be suspended` month `the month in which the pensioner left Canada` `the month in which the person became a pensioner` `the month in which the pensioner returns to Canada` MEANS
        `the first day of the month containing` month AT LEAST firstSuspendedMonth
    AND (CONSIDER `the month in which the pensioner returns to Canada`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
         WHEN JUST returned THEN `the first day of the month containing` month LESS THAN `the first day of the month containing` returned)
    WHERE
        -- the count starts after the later of the month of leaving and the month of becoming a pensioner; six months, then the seventh
        countedFrom MEANS `oa1: the later of two dates` (`the first day of the month containing` `the month in which the pensioner left Canada`) (`the first day of the month containing` `the month in which the person became a pensioner`)
        firstSuspendedMonth MEANS `the first day of the month that is` 7 `months after the month containing` countedFrom

-- s 9(2): no suspension where the pensioner establishes twenty years' residence when they left.
-- "may be continued": read as an entitlement once the pensioner establishes the twenty years, not as a discretion (fork OA1-F20 of NOTES.md).
-- src:202 | No suspension after 20 years residence
-- src:203 | (2) In the circumstances described in subsection (1), payment of the pension may be continued without suspension for any period the pensioner remains outside Canada if the pensioner establishes that at the time the pensioner left Canada the pensioner had resided in Canada for at least twenty years after attaining the age of eighteen years.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 9(2) (src:202-203)
GIVEN `the pensioner establishes that at the time the pensioner left Canada the pensioner had resided in Canada for at least twenty years after attaining the age of eighteen years` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(2): payment of the pension may be continued without suspension` `the pensioner establishes that at the time the pensioner left Canada the pensioner had resided in Canada for at least twenty years after attaining the age of eighteen years` MEANS
    `the pensioner establishes that at the time the pensioner left Canada the pensioner had resided in Canada for at least twenty years after attaining the age of eighteen years`

-- src:200 | Suspension of pension where pensioner leaves Canada
-- src:201 | 9 (1) Where a pensioner, having left Canada either before or after becoming a pensioner, has remained outside Canada after becoming a pensioner for six consecutive months, exclusive of the month in which the pensioner left Canada, payment of the pension for any period the pensioner continues to be absent from Canada after those six months shall be suspended, but payment may be resumed with the month in which the pensioner returns to Canada.
-- src:202 | No suspension after 20 years residence
-- src:203 | (2) In the circumstances described in subsection (1), payment of the pension may be continued without suspension for any period the pensioner remains outside Canada if the pensioner establishes that at the time the pensioner left Canada the pensioner had resided in Canada for at least twenty years after attaining the age of eighteen years.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, ss 9(1), 9(2) (src:200-203)
GIVEN `payment for the month falls to be suspended under subsection 9(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `payment of the pension may be continued without suspension under subsection 9(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(1) and (2): payment of the pension for the month is suspended because of absence` `payment for the month falls to be suspended under subsection 9(1)` `payment of the pension may be continued without suspension under subsection 9(2)` MEANS
        `payment for the month falls to be suspended under subsection 9(1)`
    AND (NOT `payment of the pension may be continued without suspension under subsection 9(2)`)

-- s 9(3): ceasing to reside in Canada. Payment is suspended "six months after the end of the month in which the pensioner ceased to
-- reside": the seventh month and after, until the month in which residence is resumed.
-- src:204 | Suspension of pension where pensioner ceases to reside in Canada
-- src:205 | (3) Where a pensioner ceases to reside in Canada, whether before or after becoming a pensioner, payment of the pension shall be suspended six months after the end of the month in which the pensioner ceased to reside in Canada, but payment may be resumed with the month in which the pensioner resumes residence in Canada.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 9(3) (src:204-205)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      -- out of range: section 21 (piece oa3): Regulations, residence in Canada
      `the month in which the pensioner ceased to reside in Canada` IS A DATE
      `the month in which the pensioner resumes residence in Canada` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(3): the pensioner has ceased to reside in Canada and payment for the month falls to be suspended` month `the month in which the pensioner ceased to reside in Canada` `the month in which the pensioner resumes residence in Canada` MEANS
        `the first day of the month containing` month AT LEAST (`the first day of the month that is` 7 `months after the month containing` `the month in which the pensioner ceased to reside in Canada`)
    AND (CONSIDER `the month in which the pensioner resumes residence in Canada`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
         WHEN JUST resumed THEN `the first day of the month containing` month LESS THAN `the first day of the month containing` resumed)

-- s 9(4): no suspension where the pensioner establishes twenty years' residence when they ceased to reside.
-- As s 9(2): "may be continued" is read as an entitlement once the twenty years are established (fork OA1-F20 of NOTES.md).
-- src:206 | No suspension where pensioner had 20 years residence in Canada
-- src:207 | (4) In the circumstances described in subsection (3), payment of the pension may be continued without suspension if the pensioner establishes that at the time the pensioner ceased to reside in Canada the pensioner had resided in Canada for at least twenty years after attaining the age of eighteen years.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 9(4) (src:206-207)
GIVEN `payment for the month falls to be suspended under subsection 9(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the pensioner establishes that at the time the pensioner ceased to reside in Canada the pensioner had resided in Canada for at least twenty years after attaining the age of eighteen years` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(3) and (4): payment of the pension for the month is suspended because the pensioner ceased to reside in Canada` `payment for the month falls to be suspended under subsection 9(3)` `the pensioner establishes that at the time the pensioner ceased to reside in Canada the pensioner had resided in Canada for at least twenty years after attaining the age of eighteen years` MEANS
        `payment for the month falls to be suspended under subsection 9(3)`
    AND (NOT `the pensioner establishes that at the time the pensioner ceased to reside in Canada the pensioner had resided in Canada for at least twenty years after attaining the age of eighteen years`)

-- s 9(5): "payment of the pension may be suspended" where the pensioner fails to comply: the Minister's judgment is an input, and
-- payment may be resumed when the pensioner has complied.
-- src:208 | Failure to comply with Act
-- src:209 | (5) Where a pensioner fails to comply with any of the provisions of this Act or the regulations, payment of the pension may be suspended, and where a pension is so suspended, payment may be resumed when the pensioner has complied with those provisions.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 9(5) (src:208-209)
GIVEN `the pensioner fails to comply with a provision of this Act or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 25 (piece oa3); section 26 (piece oa3): Regulations, notice of absence and suspension
      `the Minister decides to suspend payment of the pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the pensioner has complied with those provisions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(5): payment of the pension is suspended for failure to comply` `the pensioner fails to comply with a provision of this Act or the regulations` `the Minister decides to suspend payment of the pension` `the pensioner has complied with those provisions` MEANS
        `the pensioner fails to comply with a provision of this Act or the regulations`
    AND `the Minister decides to suspend payment of the pension`
    AND (NOT `the pensioner has complied with those provisions`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 9.1: the pensioner's request that the pension cease, and for reinstatement

-- (1) and (2): a pensioner may ask in writing; the pension ceases on the last day of the month in which the Minister approves.
-- src:210 | Request that pension cease to be payable
-- src:211 | 9.1 (1) Any pensioner may make a request to the Minister in writing that their pension cease to be payable.
-- src:212 | When pension ceases to be payable
-- src:213 | (2) A pension shall cease to be payable on the last day of the month in which the Minister approves a request under subsection (1).
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 9.1(1), s 9.1(2) (src:210-213)
GIVEN `the pensioner has made a request to the Minister in writing that their pension cease to be payable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the Minister approves the request` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 9.1(2): the last day on which the pension is payable` `the pensioner has made a request to the Minister in writing that their pension cease to be payable` `the day on which the Minister approves the request` MEANS
    IF `the pensioner has made a request to the Minister in writing that their pension cease to be payable`
    THEN (CONSIDER `the day on which the Minister approves the request`
          WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
          WHEN JUST approved THEN JUST (`the last day of the month containing` approved))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (3): a pensioner whose pension has ceased under (2) may request reinstatement in writing.
-- src:214 | Request for reinstatement
-- src:215 | (3) A pensioner whose pension has ceased to be payable under subsection (2) may make a request in writing to the Minister that their pension be reinstated.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 9.1(3) (src:214-215)
GIVEN `the pension has ceased to be payable under subsection 9.1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the pensioner makes a request in writing to the Minister that their pension be reinstated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9.1(3): the pensioner may have the pension reinstated on request` `the pension has ceased to be payable under subsection 9.1(2)` `the pensioner makes a request in writing to the Minister that their pension be reinstated` MEANS
        `the pension has ceased to be payable under subsection 9.1(2)`
    AND `the pensioner makes a request in writing to the Minister that their pension be reinstated`

-- (4): payment commences in the month following the month in which the Minister receives the request or in the month the pensioner
-- chose in the request, whichever is later.
-- src:216 | When reinstatement effective
-- src:217 | (4) A pension shall be reinstated and payment shall commence in the month following the month in which the Minister receives a request under subsection (3) or in the month chosen by the pensioner in the request, whichever is later.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 9.1(4) (src:216-217)
GIVEN `the day on which the Minister receives the request` IS A DATE
      `the month chosen by the pensioner in the request` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 9.1(4): the month in which payment of the reinstated pension commences` `the day on which the Minister receives the request` `the month chosen by the pensioner in the request` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the month chosen by the pensioner in the request`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN followingMonth
    WHEN JUST chosen THEN `oa1: the later of two dates` followingMonth (`the first day of the month containing` chosen)
    WHERE
        followingMonth MEANS `the first day of the month that is` 1 `months after the month containing` `the day on which the Minister receives the request`

-- The pension is payable for a month unless s 9.1 has made it cease and not yet reinstated it: it ceases after the last day of the
-- month of approval and is payable again from the month in which payment commences after reinstatement.
-- src:210 | Request that pension cease to be payable
-- src:211 | 9.1 (1) Any pensioner may make a request to the Minister in writing that their pension cease to be payable.
-- src:212 | When pension ceases to be payable
-- src:213 | (2) A pension shall cease to be payable on the last day of the month in which the Minister approves a request under subsection (1).
-- src:214 | Request for reinstatement
-- src:215 | (3) A pensioner whose pension has ceased to be payable under subsection (2) may make a request in writing to the Minister that their pension be reinstated.
-- src:216 | When reinstatement effective
-- src:217 | (4) A pension shall be reinstated and payment shall commence in the month following the month in which the Minister receives a request under subsection (3) or in the month chosen by the pensioner in the request, whichever is later.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 9.1 (src:210-217)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `the last day on which the pension is payable` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the month in which payment of the reinstated pension commences` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9.1: the pension has not ceased to be payable for the month` month `the last day on which the pension is payable` `the month in which payment of the reinstated pension commences` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day on which the pension is payable`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST last THEN
        (`the first day of the month containing` month AT MOST `the first day of the month containing` last)
        OR (CONSIDER `the month in which payment of the reinstated pension commences`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST reinstated THEN `the first day of the month containing` month AT LEAST `the first day of the month containing` reinstated)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 9.2: resumption after incarceration

-- src:218 | Resumption of pension
-- src:219 | 9.2 Payment of a pension that is suspended by virtue of subsection 5(3) shall resume in respect of the month in which a pensioner is released but only after they notify the Minister in writing before or after their release.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 9.2 (src:218-219)
GIVEN `payment of the pension is suspended by virtue of subsection 5(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the pensioner is released` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the pensioner notifies the Minister in writing, before or after their release` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 9.2: the month in respect of which payment of the pension resumes` `payment of the pension is suspended by virtue of subsection 5(3)` `the day on which the pensioner is released` `the pensioner notifies the Minister in writing, before or after their release` MEANS
    IF `payment of the pension is suspended by virtue of subsection 5(3)` AND `the pensioner notifies the Minister in writing, before or after their release`
    THEN (CONSIDER `the day on which the pensioner is released`
          WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
          WHEN JUST released THEN JUST (`the first day of the month containing` released))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 9.3: request to cancel the pension

-- (1): "in the prescribed manner and within the prescribed time after payment of a pension has commenced". The register input
-- `the prescribed time within which a request for cancellation may be made` is a Time limit (Regulations s 26.1(1): six months).
-- src:220 | Request to cancel pension
-- src:221 | 9.3 (1) A pensioner may, in the prescribed manner and within the prescribed time after payment of a pension has commenced, request cancellation of that pension.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 9.3(1) (src:220-221)
GIVEN `the request is made in the prescribed manner` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 26.1(1) (piece oa3): Regulations
      `the day on which payment of the pension commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the request is made` IS A DATE
      -- out of range: section 26.1(1) (piece oa3): Regulations, six months
      `the prescribed time within which a request for cancellation may be made` IS A `Time limit`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9.3(1): the pensioner may request cancellation of the pension` `the request is made in the prescribed manner` `the day on which payment of the pension commenced` `the day on which the request is made` `the prescribed time within which a request for cancellation may be made` MEANS
        `the request is made in the prescribed manner`
    AND `the day on which the request is made` AT LEAST `the day on which payment of the pension commenced`
    AND `the day on which the request is made` AT MOST (`the day that is` `the prescribed time within which a request for cancellation may be made` `after` `the day on which payment of the pension commenced`)

-- (2): the request is granted and the pension, with any related supplement and allowance, is repaid within the prescribed time
-- (Regulations s 26.1(2): six months after the day the request is granted): the application is deemed never to have been made
-- and the pension is deemed not to have been payable for the period.
-- src:222 | Effect of cancellation
-- src:223 | (2) If the request is granted and the amount of any pension and related supplement and allowance is repaid within the prescribed time,
-- src:224 | (a) the application for that pension is deemed never to have been made; and
-- src:225 | (b) the pension is deemed for the purposes of this Act not to have been payable during the period in question.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 9.3(2) (src:222-225)
GIVEN `the request is granted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the request is granted` IS A DATE
      -- out of range: section 18.2 (piece oa2): the supplement, repaid with the pension and the allowance
      `the day on which the amount of any pension and related supplement and allowance is repaid` IS A MAYBE DATE
      -- out of range: section 26.1(2) (piece oa3): Regulations, six months
      `the prescribed time within which the amount must be repaid` IS A `Time limit`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9.3(2): the application is deemed never to have been made and the pension is deemed not to have been payable` `the request is granted` `the day on which the request is granted` `the day on which the amount of any pension and related supplement and allowance is repaid` `the prescribed time within which the amount must be repaid` MEANS
        `the request is granted`
    AND (CONSIDER `the day on which the amount of any pension and related supplement and allowance is repaid`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST repaid THEN repaid AT MOST (`the day that is` `the prescribed time within which the amount must be repaid` `after` `the day on which the request is granted`))
